Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): contain bad config and refuse unroutable pickup
 before import [daveey]

Root (happened): strict assignee config reads escaped the preclaim gate and pickup omitted that same gate before import. Root (not caught): existing admission fixtures used valid configs and did not exercise repeated two-gateway pickup ticks. Contain config failures per card and evaluate replica history before import/budget, retaining review and quota custody.

Proof: unchanged independent probes 0 passed/4 failed before repair, 4/0 after. Real sibling-dispatch/config recovery and four-tick zero-import/eligible-peer recovery controls pass. Stable 254-file sweep 5625 passed/3 failed/1 skipped; three failures were receipt-only Mock/None replica seams. Isolate that unrelated seam only in those fixtures; final four whole files 26 passed/0 failed, retries OFF. Full scripts/check 21 gates green. Fleet remediation, deployment and original full acceptance remain open.
